pub const PRIVACY_TEXT: [Text; 57] = [
    "Last changed 30 October 2026.",
    "# In short",
    "wrela.dev is free. It shows no ads, sells nothing, and never sells or rents anything about you to anyone.",
    "We built accounts to know as little about you as we can. We don't ask for your email, your name, your age or where you are. We never see a password. We don't show ads and we don't use anyone else's analytics.",
    "You can play every game without an account. Then nothing about you leaves your device.",
    "# What we keep, and only this",
    "- An account number and an account handle: random numbers we make. The handle is what your passkey knows your account by.",
    "- Your passkey's public key, its credential ID, its signature counter, and when it was added and last used. The private key never leaves your device; we never see it.",
    "- Your account's name: four numbers that pick words from our lists. You never type it.",
    "- Your recovery codes, only as fingerprints (SHA-256 hashes), so a copy of our records can't be used to sign in.",
    "- One session cookie, which your browser keeps for wrela.dev and sends only there; no script can read it, ours included. Our server keeps its fingerprint, with when the session began and was last seen. It keeps you signed in. Games never see it. While you sign in or add a passkey, a second cookie holds that sign-in's token for at most five minutes. We use no other cookies.",
    "- A short-lived token for each game you play while signed in, which can only submit runs. We keep its fingerprint for an hour.",
    "- Your runs: the buttons you pressed, tick by tick (a replay), the time and category our server works out from them, and when you uploaded each one.",
    "- How many runs you uploaded in the past hour, and fingerprints of the replays you uploaded, to stop the same run being sent twice.",
    "- Times on our server's own clock, for when each of these was made.",
    "# What we never keep",
    "- No email address, phone number, real name or typed name of any kind.",
    "- No password.",
    "- No chat, messages or other free text.",
    "- No photos, voice or video.",
    "- No location.",
    "- No IP addresses. Our server program is never told your IP address. Cloudflare (below) sees it, as any host must, to deliver each request, and our Worker uses it for one thing: counting each address's requests over a minute, to limit how fast anyone can try to sign in. It is never written down or logged.",
    "- No third-party analytics, advertising, tracking pixels or social buttons.",
    "# What we use identifiers for",
    "The account number, the account handle, the passkey's credential ID and the session and game tokens are persistent identifiers. We use them only to:",
    "- sign you in, keep you signed in, and let you sign out or end a session elsewhere;",
    "- show your verified runs on the leaderboards under your account's name;",
    "- check uploaded runs, enforce the upload limits, and stop cheating and abuse;",
    "- keep the service secure and working, and find and fix its faults;",
    "- give you a copy of your data, and delete it when you ask.",
    "We never use them to show ads, to build a profile of you, to follow you across other sites, or to contact you.",
    "# Lines we don't cross",
    "Each of these would mean collecting personal information, and so a new design and, for children, a parent's verified consent first. We won't do any of them without changing this policy first:",
    "- asking for an email address or a phone number;",
    "- letting anyone type a name, a message or anything else;",
    "- chat, voice or video, including video of runs;",
    "- precise location;",
    "- third-party analytics, ads or social sign-in;",
    "- using an identifier for anything beyond the list above;",
    "- keeping IP addresses.",
    "# Who helps us run it",
    "- Cloudflare serves the website and runs our server, and stores its records and their backups. It sees the IP address of each visit and connection, as any web host does.",
    "- GitHub holds the source code. It never receives account data.",
    "Each acts on our behalf, and none of them gets your account's records to use for itself.",
    "# How long we keep it",
    "We keep your account's records until you delete the account. A session ends after 90 days, or when you sign out or end it; a game's token after an hour. A deleted account's records go from our server at once, and from the backups within [30 days: to be set with the backup's retention].",
    "# Your choices",
    "- Export: Account, then Export my data, gives you everything above as a JSON file.",
    "- Delete: Account, then Delete account, deletes your passkeys' records, sessions, recovery codes, runs and name at once. You'll be asked to sign in with your passkey first.",
    "# Children",
    "We don't ask anyone's age. wrela.dev is designed so that it doesn't collect personal information from anyone, children included: names are generated, nothing can be typed, and nothing above identifies a person. If you think we hold something we shouldn't, write to us and we will delete it.",
    "# Security",
    "Sign-in uses passkeys, checked on our server against the passkey's public key. Secrets are kept only as fingerprints. Every request that changes your account is checked against your session.",
    "# Changes",
    "If we change this policy, we will put the new date at the top and say on this page what changed before the change takes effect.",
    "# Contact",
    "Write to [contact address, to be added before launch]. This page is a draft for a lawyer's review and is not yet in force.",
]

